# Shopify Dev MCP Server for Polaris

## Setup

The MCP server launches via: `npx -y @shopify/dev-mcp@latest`

For integrated environments, add this configuration:
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "shopify-dev-mcp": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@shopify/dev-mcp@latest"]
    }
  }
}
```

**Requirements:** Node.js 20+ and an "LLM-enabled development environment that's capable of integrating with Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers."

## Tools & Guidance

The documentation doesn't explicitly list specific tools exposed by the MCP server. However, it emphasizes instructing your AI agent to "use available tools that help you build with web components across all supported surfaces"—including App Home, Admin UI extensions, Checkout UI extensions, Customer Account UI extensions, and POS UI extensions.

The guidance implies the server provides component-related tooling (potentially including validation capabilities), though exact tool names aren't detailed in this source material.

